## 1. Detail

This is Attempt 2 for PR #16 on branch `lab/crawdad-ground-v1` in worktree `/tmp/wt-ground-v1`. All edits remain uncommitted in the working tree for parent review.

### Summary of Changes

1. **Blocker 1 — No-Code Revisions ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L539-L551), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L643-L654), [test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py#L276-L318))**:
   - In both Arms G and C, when a revision completion produces no code block (`code_rev is None` or empty), the runner records a distinct stop reason `"no_code"` (separate from `"repeat_code"` and `"max_turns"`).
   - The arm's final module (`code`) and selected turn (`selected_turn`) retain the last non-empty module produced (never allowing `None` to overwrite the final program).
   - Added unit test `test_no_code_revision_preserves_last_non_empty_code` verifying both arms retain turn 0's code with stop reason `"no_code"`.

2. **Blocker 2 — Hard Token Cap Guarantee ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L460-L471), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L521-L524), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L625-L628), [test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py#L320-L349))**:
   - Implemented a unified pre-call hard cap rule across both arms: before **every** completion call (test-write in G, revision calls in G, and revision calls in C), if `tokens_so_far + debate.MAX_TOKENS > TASK_BUDGET` (24,576), the call is skipped with stop reason `"budget"`.
   - If test generation is skipped due to budget, `test_gen` is logged with `tests = None` and `err = "budget"`, and the loop proceeds under static and visible checks only.
   - Added unit test `test_hard_token_cap_guarantee` driving both arms with a fake model returning full `MAX_TOKENS` (6,144) on every call, asserting recorded `total_tokens` $\le 24,576$ (exactly 24,576) for both G and C.

3. **Blocker 3 — Report Summary Path Bug ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L791-L794), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L887), [test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py#L393-L455))**:
   - Fixed the variable shadowing bug in `report()` where loop boolean `sp` in the union check shadowed summary file path `sp = paths(root, label)[2]`. Renamed the loop variable to `passed_union`.
   - Added end-to-end test suite `TestReportEndToEnd.test_report_verdicts_and_summary_file` verifying `summary.json` is written to disk, parses validly, and produces each verdict (`keep`, `drop`, `inconclusive`, `no_room`) on constructed tables.

4. **Blocker 4 — Status Next-Session Line & Units ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L713), [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L162), [test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py#L457-L473))**:
   - Changed `status_line()` to invite the first seat in `ORDER` that still owes work: `nxt = next(s for s in ORDER if owe[s] > 0)`.
   - Corrected docs expected status line to `owed {'qwen32': 0, 'r1d32': 270}; next session: invite r1d32`.
   - Clarified the unit in code and spec: each task requires 3 actions (`turn0`, `arm_g`, `arm_c`), yielding 90 tasks $\times$ 3 actions = 270 actions owed per seat.
   - Added unit test `TestStatusInviteOrder` covering both cases (qwen32 owes -> invite qwen32; only r1d32 owes -> invite r1d32).

5. **Blocker 5 — Primary Contrast Execution Feedback Isolation ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L56-L65), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L204-L219), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L590-L599), [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L819-L866), [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L55-L95))**:
   - **Scoring**: Both Arms G and C are scored in the primary contrast strictly on their **LAST non-empty module**. Best-of-N selection across static, visible, and model tests is logged and evaluated as a secondary "package" result (G-best-of-N), alongside G-best-of-N vs P. No keep/drop verdict is derived from secondary results.
   - **Unified Prompt Instruction**: Both arms receive the identical `REVISION_INSTRUCTION` ("Review your solution against all requirements and constraints in the specification, and write a corrected complete module.") followed by `REVISION_SUFFIX`. The only difference is that Arm G's prompt includes the execution failure block (`Execution error:\n```\n{err}\n```\n\n`) when an error exists.
   - **Stop Rules**: Both arms share `budget`, `max_turns`, `no_code`, and `repeat_code`. Arm G alone retains `all_pass` because stopping when all static, visible, and model tests pass is execution information provided by sandbox execution.
   - **Test-Write Call**: Kept G-only and explicitly specified as part of G's treatment, counting directly against G's 24,576 completion-token budget.
   - **Protocol Hash**: Recomputed and updated to **`a7efb2060615`** in [ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L98) and [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L83).

6. **Nits**:
   - **Leak Guard ([test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py#L99-L248))**: Broadened `ExplodingTask` to raise on `tests`/`ref` access via `__getitem__`, `.get()`, `.items()`, `.values()`, `.keys()`, `__iter__()`, `.copy()`, and `__contains__()`. Tested the revision path where turn 0 fails visible tests. Added `test_prompts_never_leak_hidden_content` verifying that during all turns/arms, no prompt receives hidden tests lines, ref substrings $\ge 20$ chars, or `"104729"`, and that `step` never accesses hidden fields.
   - **Static Tier Specification ([ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py#L138), [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L68))**: Documented that `pyflakes` remains optional and absent on this machine; the active static tier consists of compile + `deny_check` + entry points check.
   - **Stage N Triad Placeholder ([docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L107-L111))**: Preserved as a clearly marked placeholder.
   - **Per-Family Visible Assert Counts ([docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L30-L35))**: Recomputed from `tasks_v10_visible.CHECKS` and `memring.FAMILIES["v10"]`:
     - `formats`: 237 asserts (was 236)
     - `number_theory`: 223 asserts
     - `graphs_geometry`: 140 asserts
     - `simulation_dp`: 124 asserts (was 125)
     - Total: 724 asserts across 89 tasks (1 `no_visible`: `v10_74`).
   - **Unbound Variables in Value Examples ([generate_visible.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/generate_visible.py#L201-L205), [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L38-L41))**: Documented that `v10_39_uuid_urn` and `v10_66_point_in_convex` retain only `ValueError` asserts because their value examples rely on unbound variables (`b` and `poly`).
   - **GPU Hours Recomputation ([docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md#L113-L143))**:
     - Per-reply time: $24,593\text{ s} / 108\text{ replies} = 227.713\text{ s} \approx 227.7\text{ s}$ per reply from stored `crawdad-v8-d2`.
     - Turn 0 solo pass rate: $13/60 \approx 21.67\%$ (qwen32 9/30, r1d32 4/30). Failing units = $180 \times (47/60) = 141$ units; passing units = 39 units.
     - Turn 0 (P): 180 replies $\times 227.7\text{ s} = 11.39$ GPU hours.
     - Arm G expected: test generation (180 $\times 75\text{ s} = 3.75\text{ h}$) + failing revisions ($141 \times 1.4\text{ revs} \times 227.7\text{ s} = 12.49\text{ h}$) = $16.24$ GPU hours (or 23.88 h with conservative 227.7 s test-write). Worst case: 45.54 GPU hours.
     - Arm C expected: all units revise on turn 1, averaging 1.2 revisions ($180 \times 1.2 \times 227.7\text{ s} = 13.66$ GPU hours). Worst case: 34.16 GPU hours.
     - Total decode GPU hours: Expected $\approx$ **41.29 GPU hours** (worst case: **91.09 GPU hours**). Swap overhead: 2 sessions $\times$ 1.3 min = 2.6 min.

